WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:04.240
Okay.

00:04.280 --> 00:05.640
So what is our function?

00:05.680 --> 00:09.840
It can go and convert all the characters of a string to an uppercase.

00:09.840 --> 00:11.440
It's going to make everything capitalize.

00:11.440 --> 00:13.760
And the lower function is exactly the opposite.

00:13.800 --> 00:16.880
It's going to go and convert everything to a lowercase.

00:16.880 --> 00:19.760
So let's have very simple example for those two functions okay.

00:19.800 --> 00:22.240
So now we have like three values with different cases.

00:22.240 --> 00:27.120
The first one where you have only the first character capitalized and the rest is lowercase, and then

00:27.120 --> 00:29.280
the same value, but everything is lowercase.

00:29.280 --> 00:32.600
And a third one where you have everything with an uppercase.

00:32.600 --> 00:37.120
Now if you go and apply the function upper to those three values, what's going to happen for the first

00:37.120 --> 00:40.320
value is going to go and turn it into an uppercase.

00:40.320 --> 00:44.600
So everything is going to be capitalized, not only the first character and now for the second value,

00:44.640 --> 00:47.440
it's going to turn it as well to completely capitalized.

00:47.440 --> 00:49.360
So all the characters gonna change.

00:49.360 --> 00:52.040
And for the last value it is already capitalized.

00:52.040 --> 00:53.920
So in the output you will get the same value.

00:53.920 --> 00:55.720
So actually nothing can happen for that.

00:55.720 --> 00:57.440
So this is simply the uppercase.

00:57.440 --> 01:02.200
Now let's see what can happen if you use the lowercase for the first value, only the first character

01:02.200 --> 01:03.040
is going to be changed.

01:03.040 --> 01:05.320
And then you will have everything in lowercase.

01:05.320 --> 01:07.920
The second value it is already a lowercase value.

01:07.920 --> 01:10.280
So if you apply lowercase, nothing can happen.

01:10.280 --> 01:11.400
You will get the same value.

01:11.400 --> 01:16.090
But for the last one, everything here is capitalized and if you apply lowercase, all the characters

01:16.130 --> 01:17.810
can convert to a lowercase.

01:17.810 --> 01:19.610
So my friends, this is very simple.

01:19.610 --> 01:22.050
Let's go back to SQL in order to practice that.

01:22.090 --> 01:27.890
Okay, so we have the following task and it says transform the customer's first name to lowercase.

01:27.890 --> 01:29.810
So now as you can see the first names here.

01:29.810 --> 01:31.530
The first character is a capital.

01:31.570 --> 01:33.210
The rest is lowercase.

01:33.210 --> 01:37.010
So now in this task we have to convert the whole thing into lowercase.

01:37.010 --> 01:38.330
So let's go and do that.

01:38.370 --> 01:38.970
It's very simple.

01:38.970 --> 01:44.410
We're going to say lower first name and let's go and call it low name.

01:44.410 --> 01:45.210
So that's it.

01:45.210 --> 01:46.530
Let's go and execute it.

01:46.570 --> 01:51.490
Now if we go and compare the lower name with the first name, you can see all the characters now in

01:51.530 --> 01:52.370
the lowercase.

01:52.370 --> 01:53.730
So that's it for the task.

01:53.730 --> 01:56.410
We have transformed the first name to lowercase.

01:56.410 --> 01:56.810
All right.

01:56.810 --> 01:58.570
The next task is exactly the opposite.

01:58.610 --> 02:02.090
Transform the customer's first name to uppercase.

02:02.090 --> 02:03.970
So let's go and have a new column.

02:03.970 --> 02:05.490
We're going to say upper.

02:05.890 --> 02:10.530
Then the first name as app name.

02:10.530 --> 02:11.290
So that's it.

02:11.290 --> 02:11.970
It's very simple.

02:11.970 --> 02:12.970
Let's go and execute.

02:13.010 --> 02:16.130
Now you can see in the output we have a new column called App Name.

02:16.130 --> 02:20.930
And inside it we have the first name but now all the characters in uppercase.

02:20.930 --> 02:25.290
So this is how you convert the case to lower or to upper in SQL okay.

02:25.330 --> 02:27.170
So that's all about the upper and the lower.

02:27.210 --> 02:29.610
Next we're going to talk about very interesting function.

02:29.610 --> 02:30.610
It is the trim.
